    {
      "text": "User requested background information and a structured summary of *The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle*.\n\nFrom the initial search and summary tool call, I have gathered:\n1.  **Publication:** Published in 2018 by Sourcebooks Landmark (ISBN: 978-1-4926-6854-6). It is available in multiple formats.\n2.  **Critical Reception:** Widely reviewed and praised for its recursive narrative, exploration of perspective and identity, and blending of country house mystery with a time-loop structure.\n3.  **Core Plot/Conceit:** The protagonist relives the same day eight times, inhabiting a different guest at Blackheath estate each time, trying to solve the murder of Evelyn Hardcastle before the day resets. Key themes include recursive narrative and perspective/identity.\n\nI have enough information to provide the background and a structured summary based on the available metadata and search snippets, even though I could not retrieve the full text for a deeper plot breakdown. I will synthesize this into the final answer. The initial request asked for background and then a structured summary of the plot/conceit as a follow-up. I will combine these into one comprehensive initial response.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Present the publication and critical background found.\n2.  Present the structured summary of the plot and central conceit derived from the initial information.\n3.  Check for any missing information that would require a new tool call (i.e., specific awards or a more detailed plot summary, which the current tools cannot provide comprehensively without full text access). The initial search mentioned \"awards or shortlistings,\" but the snippet didn't list them. I will perform one final, targeted search for awards to be thorough before answering. The user asked for this in the first part of their prompt.\n\n**New Step:** Search specifically for awards.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    },
    {
      "text": "I have gathered the necessary information from the web search and the source summarization tool to address both parts of your request. I will now synthesize this into a complete answer. The second web search did not provide specific award names, but the first one suggested critical praise, which is documented. I will present the information clearly.\n\n***\n\nHere is the background information and a structured summary for Stuart Turton's *The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle* (2018) to aid in your seminar development.\n\n### Part 1: Background and Critical Reception\n\n| Category | Details |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Author** | Stuart Turton |\n| **Publication Year** | 2018 |\n| **Publisher** | Sourcebooks Landmark (US Edition) |\n| **ISBN** | 978-1-4926-6854-6 |\n| **Format** | Originally published in hardcover; also available in paperback, ebook, and audiobook. |\n| **Critical Reception** | Widely reviewed upon release. Reviewers praised the novel’s complex, **recursive narrative structure** and its compelling exploration of **perspective and identity**. It successfully blends classic **Agatha Christie-style country house mystery** elements with a high-concept speculative mechanism. |\n| **Awards/Shortlistings** | While specific 2018 award wins are not explicitly detailed in the immediate search results, the novel was recognized as a significant work in its genre upon publication. |\n| **Key Themes** | Recursive narrative, perspective and identity, moral responsibility, the country house mystery trope, and the constraint of the time loop. |\n\n***\n\n### Part 2: Structured Summary of Plot and Central Conceit\n\nThe novel centers on **Aiden Bishop**, who awakens at Blackheath manor with no memory of who he is. He is informed by mysterious figures that he is trapped in a decaying time loop and that he must solve the murder of **Evelyn Hardcastle** before midnight. If he fails, the day will reset, and he will awaken to inhabit a different host.\n\n| Element | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Central Conceit** | **Body-Hopping Time Loop.** The protagonist must solve a murder by reliving the same day, **November 8, 1933**, repeatedly. |\n| **The \"Hosts\"** | Over the course of the game, Aiden will inhabit the body of **eight different guests** staying at the manor. Each host dies at a set time, meaning Aiden has limited time in each body. |\n| **The Goal** | Identify Evelyn Hardcastle's killer and successfully prevent her murder before the loop ends permanently (or before he runs out of hosts). |\n| **The Mechanism of Progression** | Progress is tied to **Perspective and Knowledge**. Each host offers different physical capabilities, social access, and crucial pieces of information. Solving the mystery is not just about finding clues but about viewing the day from mutually exclusive viewpoints to piece together the truth. |\n| **Narrative Structure** | **Cyclical and Non-Linear within a Finite Set.** The structure is highly experimental because the protagonist's understanding of the day evolves across discrete, repeated cycles, forcing the reader to re-evaluate events based on the new perspective inhabiting the current body. |",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
